{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Happy are those whose way is perfect</b> — These one hundred and seventy-six verses, which are alef-bet, the Master of the Masorah has already mentioned that there is no verse that does not contain there a mention of דרך or תורה or עדות or פקודים or אמירה or חוק or מצוה or משפט or דבר, except one verse, and it is ערוב עבדך לטוב. And I have already mentioned at the beginning of the book what the commentators said regarding these verses, for some say that David did not compose them." "<b>Happy, way</b> — It serves another, and likewise it is ההולכים בדרך תורת ה' (those who walk in the way of the Torah of YHWH)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 119, :notes {0 "Resolved בעל המסורה as 'the Master of the Masorah' rather than identifying a specific figure, since Ibn Ezra uses the epithet generically."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:40:09.603580513Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}